 "article": {
  "title": "The Gig Economy: Freedom or Uncertainty?",
  "topic": "经济（零工经济）",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 225,
  "paras": [
   "Ten years ago, a young designer in a big city would usually look for a full-time job in a company. Today, she may well earn a living by taking on short projects from an app. This kind of work is often called the “gig economy,” and it has grown astonishingly fast.",
   "The appeal is easy to understand. Gig workers can choose when and where to work, take up several different projects at the same time, and earn money with nothing more than a phone and a laptop. For students, parents and people between jobs, that flexibility can be a real lifeline.",
   "Yet the picture is not entirely bright. Most gig workers are not employees but independent contractors, which means they receive no paid holidays, no sick leave and no pension from the platform. Their income can rise sharply one month and fall the next, and when a dispute arises, they often find that nobody is clearly responsible.",
   "Governments and platforms are now searching for a middle way. Some countries have created a special legal status that gives gig workers a few basic protections without making them full employees. Others require platforms to be more open about how pay is calculated. The debate is far from settled, but one thing is clear: as more people work this way, the rules that protect them must keep pace."
  ],
  "zh": "十年前，大城市的年轻设计师通常会去公司找一份全职工作；如今，她很可能靠在手机上接短项目来谋生——这就是“零工经济”，它发展得惊人地快。它的吸引力在于自由：自己决定何时何地工作、可以同时接多个项目、一部手机一台电脑就能挣钱，对学生、家长和处于职业空档期的人来说尤其如此。但前景并非全然光明：多数零工不是雇员而是独立的承揽人，平台不给带薪假、病假和养老金，收入忽高忽低，一旦发生纠纷往往找不到明确的责任方。各国政府和平台正在寻找折中的办法，比如设立一种“中间身份”给予基本保障，或要求平台公开计酬方式。争论远未结束，但有一点很清楚：越多人以这种方式工作，保护他们的规则就越要跟上。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "Most gig workers are not employees but independent contractors, which means they receive no paid holidays, no sick leave and no pension from the platform.",
    "cn": "多数零工不是雇员，而是独立的承揽人，这意味着他们拿不到带薪休假、病假，也得不到平台提供的养老金。",
    "why": "which 引导非限制性定语从句，指代前面整句话（而不是某一个名词），相当于“而这一点意味着……”。写作时可用来对前面的事实作解释或小结。"
   },
   {
    "en": "as more people work this way, the rules that protect them must keep pace.",
    "cn": "随着越来越多的人以这种方式工作，保护他们的规则也必须跟上。",
    "why": "as 引导时间/原因状语从句，表示“随着……”；the rules that protect them 中 that 引导定语从句修饰 rules。句式适合用于议论文结尾，表达“随形势变化，制度要跟进”。"
   }
